  "setup": "Plugin open on Main, test chat. A page-side frame watcher (requestAnimationFrame loop, f1-watch.js idea; kept only in the page, removed at the end) logged every frame where the focused element's label, rect or the pane's scrollTop changed, with a timestamp. After each press a page call waited until 2.1 s had passed since the last logged change, then read the log, so every press has its 0.2 s and 1.8 s state: 'scrollTop_first_frame' is the first changed frame, 'scrollTop_settled' the last. Press and read were separate tool calls. D-pad only; no A anywhere. Raw per-press files in the scratch folder: f1-settings-down.json, f1-settings-up.json, f1-developer-down.json, f1-developer-up.json, f1-raw-all.json, f1-summary.json. Press 1 on Settings Down was read with the first watcher version (no label); its rect and scroll match the later Text size pass.",
